{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Yesterday I saw Romeo and Juliet by the English troupe, — Juliet was very good, although not of the first rank, — not as much as Mde. Crelinger 2), — Romeo—Kemble was quite mediocre in the first four acts, without any life, — but in the last one, dreadful, mad, — I have now seen the English fury in its full glory; it is wonderful how they butcher Shakespeare; in the last act Juliet awakens while Romeo is still alive, but has already drunk the poison, — here is a scene in which she becomes completely out of her mind with madness and rages most horribly. — The scene of the first meeting of Romeo and Juliet is butchered in the same way, he already loves her beforehand, sits down next to her on the chair before he speaks to her, and when she is interrupted by the Nurse, Mercutio makes fun of her so that they can stay together and talk longer. —"}}],"created":1795220820,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":196,"prompt_tokens":284,"total_tokens":480,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-p68LmtXDYtXaCctLs55podoyuRfuDuqt","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":284,"prompt_ms":423.359,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.490700704225352,"prompt_per_second":670.8254696368803,"predicted_n":196,"predicted_ms":4515.662,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.157241025641028,"predicted_per_second":43.183037171515494}}